The desktop distribution bundles Electron (MIT) and Chromium and Node.js components
under their respective licenses. Electron's LICENSE.electron.txt and
LICENSES.chromium.html are included by the desktop packager.

The private merchant engine bundles CPython and standard-library components.
CPython is under the Python Software Foundation license. The bundled Python
distribution includes its license; PyInstaller is GPL-2.0-or-later with a bootloader
exception allowing distribution of applications under their own license.

TEE verification and merchant TLS sessions are implemented by teemerchant's native
library, loaded directly into the merchant engine. No teeproxy executable is bundled
or launched. The verifier source is derived from the MIT-licensed teeproxy project;
the original source revision and attribution are recorded in native/NOTICE.
Its LICENSE, NOTICE, dependency lockfile, source hashes and library hash accompany
the distribution under resources/licenses/native. Locked dependency licenses and a
manifest are included in its dependency-notices subdirectory.

No merchant identities, account credentials, TEE trust policies or deployment
configuration are included in a public desktop release.
